SUMMARY:Milky Way · Norah Head Lighthouse · Core rising beside the lighth
 ouse
LOCATION:Norah Head Rock Pool\, Bald Street\, Norah Head NSW 2263
GEO:-33.27893;151.56964
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.27893,151.56964
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The galactic core rising out of the Pacific beside Norah 
 Head Lighthouse. Early season\, so the core is low and short lived before 
 dawn. Frame the lighthouse low and let the core climb beside it.\nPriority
 : Optional\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nNight of Sat 06 Feb into Sun 07 Feb 2027
 .\nShoot window: 02:55 to 04:45 (core between 8° and 60° high\, sky full
 y dark\, moon down).\nBest composition: about 04:45\, core 29° high in th
 e ESE.\nArrive by 02:10 to set up and focus.\nSunset 19:54 · astronomical
  dusk 21:25 · astronomical dawn 04:49 · sunrise 06:21\nMoon: new moon Su
 n 07 Feb 02:56. 0% lit and below the horizon during the window. Moonrise S
 un 06:35 · Moonset Sat 19:40\n\nCORE POSITION\n03:00  altitude 9°\, azim
 uth 119° ESE\n03:30  altitude 15°\, azimuth 115° ESE\n04:00  altitude 2
 1°\, azimuth 112° ESE\n04:30  altitude 26°\, azimuth 109° ESE\n\nCAMER
 A POSITION\nNorah Head Rock Pool\, Bald Street\, Norah Head NSW 2263\nCame
 ra pin: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.27893\,151.569
 64\nSubject pin (Norah Head Lighthouse): https://www.google.com/maps/searc
 h/?api=1&query=-33.28165\,151.57635\nNorah Head Lighthouse is 693 m away o
 n bearing 116° (ESE). At 04:45 the core is 9 degrees left of it\, 29° up
 . To stack the core straight above it\, move about 104 m to your right\, k
 eeping the same distance.\nStraight line from Neutral Bay: about 70 km.\n\
 nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A1)\nFE 12-24mm F2.8 GM at 12 to 14 mm fo
 r single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM II for a sharper multi row panorama.\n12 
 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 14 mm: up to 16 s. 24 mm: up to 9 s. 35 m
 m f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nForeground: separate longer frames at ISO 
 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames from the same tripod position.\nPeak Des
 ign travel tripod\, red head torch\, dew heater strap on the lens.\n\nFIEL
 D NOTES\n- Work from the public rock platform and foreshore\, not the ligh
 thouse grounds.\n- Rock platform: check swell and tide first. Wet rock is 
 slippery in the dark.\n- Light from the lighthouse beam sweeps the frame. 
 Time exposures between passes or blend.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (
 camera pin\, subject pin and time set): https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll
 =-33.27893\,151.56964&center=-33.27893\,151.56964&z=15&dt=2027-02-06T17%3A
 45%3A00.000Z&sll=-33.28165\,151.57635&fovb=115.9&fovhfov=104.10&fovvfov=81
 .20&fovd=693&fovo=l&fovov=1\nPhotoPills: Planner > drop the pin at the cam
 era coordinates > set the date and time above > Milky Way layer. Use Night
  AR on site to confirm the core path.\nCheck cloud (BOM and Windy) and lig
 ht pollution (lightpollutionmap.info) two days out.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon phase
 s: US Naval Observatory 2027 table (aa.usno.navy.mil).\nSun\, moon and cor
 e positions: computed with Skyfield and JPL DE421 for the camera pin.\nCoo
 rdinates: OpenStreetMap. Terrain horizons: SRTM 30 m via OpenTopoData.
CATEGORIES:Astrophotography
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
