GEO:-33.52379;150.07734
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.52379,150.07734
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The core rising in the east south east above the eastern 
 arm of Lake Lyell. From this shoreline the water runs 100 m to 600 m out t
 oward the core. Calm nights give a reflection.\nPriority: Very high\n\nWHE
 N (Sydney time)\nNight of Sat 08 May into Sun 09 May 2027.\nShoot window: 
 20:03 to 00:18 (core between 8° and 60° high\, sky fully dark\, moon dow
 n).\nBest composition: about 21:58\, core 30° high in the ESE.\nArrive by
