 52379\,150.07734\nFace ESE (azimuth 107°) at 21:58.\nStraight line from N
 eutral Bay: about 111 km.\n\nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A1)\nFE 12-24
 mm F2.8 GM at 12 to 14 mm for single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM II for a shar
 per multi row panorama. Dark site option: Esprit 80ED on the AM5N with the
  ASI2600MC Air for the Lagoon and Trifid region near the core. Antlia Trib
 and for the emission nebulae.\n12 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 14 mm: 
 up to 16 s. 24 mm: up to 9 s. 35 mm f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nForegrou
 nd: separate longer frames at ISO 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames from t
 he same tripod position.\nPeak Design travel tripod\, red head torch\, dew
  heater strap on the lens.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- The park has powered and unpo
 wered camp sites. Camping is the simplest way to be on the shore after dar
 k.\n- Expect cold\, damp air in May at 790 m. Run the dew heater on lenses
  too.\n- Low hills across the lake sit about 3 degrees high\, so the core 
 clears them early.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject 
 pin and time set): https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-33.52379\,150.07734
